{
  "case": "mixed_deriv_accum",
  "pipeline_kind": "mms_convergence",
  "description": "Solved-trajectory Layer-C case for mixed_deriv_2nd_uniform = grad(grad(u,y),x) = d2u/dxdy. Freeze-and-accumulate pattern: u=cos(2*pi*(x+y)) is frozen (D/dt=0) and a state `acc` integrates the mixed derivative, so acc(t)=t*d2u/dxdy. Exact = t*(-(2*pi)^2)*cos(2*pi*(x+y)). Freeze-accumulate sidesteps the non-parabolic (indefinite-spectrum) instability of integrating the bare mixed operator. The field-level pipeline (build_ode_problem) sweeps N=16->32 (2D periodic) and verifies O(h^2) spatial convergence.",
  "esm": "mixed_deriv_pde.esm",
  "grid_refs": [
